ace, so no rows were dropped.\n\nSQL run:\n\n```sql\nSELECT fb.card,\n       COUNT(*) AS boards,\n       AVG(s.place) AS avg_place\nFROM (SELECT DISTINCT game, seat, card\n      FROM board_units\n      WHERE round = 0 AND card IS NOT NULL) fb\nJOIN seats s ON s.game = fb.game AND s.seat = fb.seat\nGROUP BY fb.card\nHAVING COUNT(*) >= 100\nORDER BY avg_place ASC\nLIMIT 10;\n```\n\nI used a subquery instead of a CTE because `read_query` rejected the `WITH` form.","ttft_ms":1100,"type":"result","duration_ms":9345,"uuid":"4ebeedf3-8cf3-4803-ad64-fecce94ebbfa","ttft_stream_ms":843,"time_to_request_ms":195,"first_content_frame_ms":843,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-01T03:14:59.643Z"}
